Practical NO: 7

Text Editing using vi Editor: Create and edit files using vi editor.

Theory: The vi editor is a text editor in Linux used to create, edit, save and delete text in files.

Requirements:

•Linux / Ubuntu Terminal
•vi editor
•Basic knowledge of vi modes and commands.

a) Open and create a file using vi.

$ vi notes.txt : Creates a new file named notes.txt or open it if it already exist.

b) Work in Insert mode and command mode

i : Enters Insert Mode to type or edit text.

Esc : Returns from Insert Mode to command Mode.

c) Save and exit the file

:w : Saves the file.

:q : Exits the vi editor.

:wq : Saves the file and exits vi.

d) Edit and delete text using basic vi commands.

x : Deletes the character under the cursor.

dd : Deletes the current lines.

u : Undo the last change.

r : Replace the character under the cursor.
